build/
build*/
out/
.vs/
.vscode/ipch/
*.user
*.suo
*.log
# CMakeLists.txt IS COMMITTED, both the generated root one and the hand-written host's.
#
# It is generated from cmake.toml by cmkr, which is exactly why it used to be ignored -- but that
# made a fresh clone unbuildable without cmkr on PATH, and cmkr deliberately SKIPS regeneration
# when CI is set in the environment (GitHub Actions sets it), so a runner would have found no
# CMakeLists.txt and nothing willing to produce one. Committing it is what makes clone -> configure
# -> build work anywhere.
#
# The editing rule is unchanged: change cmake.toml, never CMakeLists.txt. Regeneration happens on
# any local build (build.bat clears CI); commit the regenerated file in the SAME commit as the
# cmake.toml change, or CI builds the previous project definition and says nothing.
# reload copies made by the injector sit next to the built DLL
fear2vr.*.dll
*.pyc

# Frame captures and files created by a mangled CLI argument being taken
# as an output path -- a 36 MB '--info' BMP reached origin this way.
*.bmp
*.png
--*

# staging/ IS the payload -- it is committed on purpose. A global core.excludesFile with *.dll in it
# (this machine has one) would otherwise drop d3d9.dll silently, so the repo says so itself: a repo
# .gitignore outranks the global one, and a CI runner that has no global ignore behaves identically.
!staging/*.dll

# the CI bundle, assembled from build outputs -- never a source
dist/
